{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/168407-20th-anniversary-books","id":168407,"title":"20th Anniversary Books","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-13T17:59:02-07:00","id":168407,"title":"20th Anniversary Books","content":"I picked up Vampire and Werewolf, but haven't really had a chance to read them cover-to-cover. I had read that they basically just reprint the original games (as opposed to updating to the new rules), but that they included a few &quot;tweaks&quot;. <br /> <br /> I'mjust wondering if anything was done to make crossovers between systems work a bit more smoothly, or if it's still wonky?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2178-arnabas","name":"Arnabas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T18:31:46-07:00","id":168464,"title":"","content":"The Anniversary Editions are whole new editions of the games, and mostly have brand new material. They don't use the newer World of Darkness system, but they do take some cues from it here and there. The biggest differences are that the metaplots aren't as intrinsic. The setting is more neutral and open. The background is still fairly in depth, but it doesn't whack you over the head with it (not nearly as much &quot;The prince of Pittsburgh was killed by the Bishop of Philadelphia so now the Ventrue Archon...&quot;) . M20 may well end up being the odd one out, in a way, since the mechanics are getting a fair sized revision, with a lot of different options from the various editions. As for crossovers, there isn't much accounting for it. Each Anniversary Edition is its own beast, and that may or may not work for crossovers, depending on the table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 06-13-2014, 09:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T08:20:47-07:00","id":168944,"title":"","content":"It's going to be like before. It takes special books for crossovers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T10:44:18-07:00","id":169915,"title":"","content":"My understanding is that the rules systems are mostly only tweaked from the Revised rules, at least for the 3 games that had Revised editions. No idea what they'll do with Wraith.<br /> <br /> I don't have any of the corebooks, so I don't know how much material in them is collected and updated and how much is brand-new. The additional books published in each 20th Anniversary line generally contain a lot of totally new material, plus some collected and updated info. Some books are entirely new such as the Werewolf and Mage cookbooks and the White Howlers Tribebook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T16:27:53-07:00","id":173300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/168407-20th-anniversary-books?p=168464#post168464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Anniversary Editions are whole new editions of the games, and mostly have brand new material.</div> </div> </div> </div>In theory, that's true, but the fact of <b>V20</b> included quite a bit of cut-and-paste from Revised Edition in the 20th book. I don't mention this as any kind of indictment, and I understand the reasons for it. White Wolf (at the time) saw the <b>Vampire: the Masquerade</b> 20th anniversary as a chance to put out a treat for those who loved the game. That treat was the <b>V20</b>, initially conceived as an omnibus of all the rules they could fit into one lovely volume. That grew into 'tweaking' some rules (most notable 'physical' Disciplines, Tremere clan weakness, fixes to some mechanics) and new art and fiction, but the book wasn't intended to be the 'new edition' that many of us currently see it as being. I'm not saying it does not deserve said designation, but when Onyx Path decided it was time that <b>Werewolf: the Apocalypse</b> got its own 20th anniversary book, we did receive a proper new edition. We should expect the same to be true for <b>Mage: the Ascension</b>, <b>Dark Ages: Vampire</b>, and <b>Wraith: the Oblivion</b> books.<br /> <br /> The above only serves to show how imprecise terms can be. To say 'whole new edition' isn't <i>exactly</i> wrong, but it's misleading when dealing with <b>V20</b> as the first of them. No doubt, I love my <b>V20</b> to pieces, but I see it as more 'Revised Plus' than the full 'Fourth Edition' that <b>W20</b> is. As ever, mileage varies, so don't feel that you gotta agree with me.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit</b>: Oh, and cross over is still not easy! Yeah, on-topic, at least at the end...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T19:39:59-07:00","id":175694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phaolan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/168407-20th-anniversary-books?p=173300#post173300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In theory, that's true, but the fact of <b>V20</b> included quite a bit of cut-and-paste from Revised Edition in the 20th book. I don't mention this as any kind of indictment, and I understand the reasons for it. White Wolf (at the time) saw the <b>Vampire: the Masquerade</b> 20th anniversary as a chance to put out a treat for those who loved the game. That treat was the <b>V20</b>, initially conceived as an omnibus of all the rules they could fit into one lovely volume. That grew into 'tweaking' some rules (most notable 'physical' Disciplines, Tremere clan weakness, fixes to some mechanics) and new art and fiction, but the book wasn't intended to be the 'new edition' that many of us currently see it as being. I'm not saying it does not deserve said designation, but when Onyx Path decided it was time that <b>Werewolf: the Apocalypse</b> got its own 20th anniversary book, we did receive a proper new edition. We should expect the same to be true for <b>Mage: the Ascension</b>, <b>Dark Ages: Vampire</b>, and <b>Wraith: the Oblivion</b> books.<br /> <br /> The above only serves to show how imprecise terms can be. To say 'whole new edition' isn't <i>exactly</i> wrong, but it's misleading when dealing with <b>V20</b> as the first of them. No doubt, I love my <b>V20</b> to pieces, but I see it as more 'Revised Plus' than the full 'Fourth Edition' that <b>W20</b> is. As ever, mileage varies, so don't feel that you gotta agree with me.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that's fair. Vampire probably needed the fewest changes of the Big Three, but I more or less agree with you--V20 Dark Ages may well offer a lot more variance than V20 did.<br /> <br /> <b>V20 </b>was definitely more conservative because it came first. I think it CAN be called a proper new edition, because of how much the tone and attitude has changed, but I agree that that's a fiddly distinction, and mileage varies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T00:56:00-07:00","id":178723,"title":"","content":"I had a look at the M20 Quickstart, and it looks like so far we have got some revisions in terminology (Magick, Paradigm, Practice, Tools, Focus) some Traditions got renamed (Society of Ether, Verbenae, Chakravanti... Akashic Brotherhood also got renamed) but thats about it. It also included a very nice list of common magickal effects and the usual Spheres required. A new chart that had to do with time, though the purpose escapes me. But thats all I noticed...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T13:35:56-07:00","id":179202,"title":"","content":"It's sort of like.... &quot;Fourth Edition: the Refinement&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment